Description: adapt build and launcher to Debian
 The self-extracting launcher is turned into a real shell script:
  - a shebang is added;
  - the C source and the binary go into a private mktemp directory,
    removed on exit, instead of the current directory (the demo deletes
    "y" and "x.c" from its working directory when it quits);
  - the code is compiled with -std=gnu89: GCC 14 rejects implicit
    declarations and GCC 15 (C23) old-style K&R definitions;
  - the sound, unsigned 8-bit mono at 8 kHz (OSS /dev/dsp defaults), is
    played with aplay instead of /dev/dsp, which needed osspd;
  - the demo runs in its own session: it ends with kill(0, SIGTERM), which
    must not reach the shell or the desktop that started it.
 The build script writes the launcher under the package name.
